{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges","id":1148179,"title":"2e Pledges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-08T17:46:33-07:00","id":1148179,"title":"2e Pledges","content":"Is it just me, or is the Pledges subsystem for Lost 2e extremely neutered from what 1e had to offer?<br /> <br /> The weak Sealing pledges that fae creatures and Changelings can more or less just ignore outright. Oaths which grant a single minor boon, and in exchange leave you permanently bound to whatever group or faction you just joined, with no way out. Bargains which require you to invest significant chunks of your character's free time into doing services for a mortal, with the only benefit being that you're slightly harder for Huntsmen to track and that the mortal might do some extremely basic favors for you in return.<br /> <br /> That's a far cry from 1e's Pledges subsystem. Flexible penalties for oath breakers, boons in the form of temporary Attributes, Skills, or Merits, supplies of Glamour for following Pledges - all of that's gone. Or, if not gone completely, then sealed behind a 'mother may I' homebrew option where you have to ask your Storyteller for permission to make something new up for your Motley's permanent Ability, instead of having options already available.<br /> <br /> Are Pledges going to get reworked from the current preview? Because as they stand, they're not bad, per se. But where 1e's Pledge subsystem was a fully-fleshed set of rules, 2e's Pledge subsystem is so underwhelming that it could probably just get replaced with some basic Oath Merits and call it a day, for what little variety and utility it actually has to offer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">For those who haven't taken the time to read it yet, here's the entire Pledge system as it currently stands - or at least the most current version I've found.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T18:25:04-07:00","id":1148188,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1974\" data-vbnamecard=\"1974\">jagadaishio</a>. I believe the document you have a link to was a preview for the David Hill manuscript of Changeling 2e, not the current manuscript from the line's present developers Rose Bailey and Meghan Fitzgerald. I don't believe the present manuscript's pledge system has been previewed yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T18:39:24-07:00","id":1148191,"title":"","content":"We've <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges\">done</a> this thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1094105-previous-pledge-procedure-problems\">twice</a> already and I don't think anyone's too eager to go for a third run at it, least of all when you've clearly already made up your mind with regards to your opening question and Robert's highlighted the principal issue with your closing question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T06:50:14-07:00","id":1148290,"title":"","content":"That's good news, and I'm glad to hear it. Hopefully whatever they've got in the works will be something other than easily-ignored, barely functional, or something that serves almost exclusively as a social hoop to jump through when joining your latest magical club. Because as it stands, Pledges might not be horrible - there's nothing unbalanced or broken about them - but they're so underwhelming that there's really no reason to interact with them except as a barrier standing between you and the story. Very little stick, and even less carrot.<br /> <br /> Have there been any blog posts with hints or clues as to what's coming for Pledges, or is it the case that, as far as we know, they might not have changed a single thing? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T07:43:31-07:00","id":1148301,"title":"","content":"I wrote pledges, both the original version that David developed and the current version that Rose/Meghan developed. Very little changed. Sorry if you don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T08:45:34-07:00","id":1148322,"title":"","content":"Ah, well, that's good to know, at least. The rules are more underwhelming than actually bad, so I'm definitely going to be adding a lot more carrot and a lot more stick in anything I run just to dial up the motivations to not-ignore them in play. I'll probably crib some of the boons and consequences from Goblin Pledges to give Sealings more of an incentive to both give and take them - in-character that is, since a Beat is always a solid enough meta-game reason.<br /> <br /> Thanks for letting me know how they're going to shake out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:23:32-07:00","id":1148351,"title":"","content":"Well, it looks like one of the main antagonists in this edition are the Huntsmen. They seem to be even more prominent than in the current edition. So having a way to keep them at bay is a good thing with bargains. I also really do like the Oaths, and the benefits they can provide. The seals just seem like a fun little thing that you can use for story fun and to help intimidate mortals or those who do not know how seals work. It is all just more of a story driven mechanic. The power and weight they carry will be as powerful and heavy as the players and ST put in them. And I guess that would be their weakest point. If you have players who are mechanics driven instead of story driven it can be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18330-redspieder","name":"Redspieder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18330_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T11:12:21-07:00","id":1148374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148290#post1148290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's good news, and I'm glad to hear it. Hopefully whatever they've got in the works will be something other than easily-ignored, barely functional, or something that serves almost exclusively as a social hoop to jump through when joining your latest magical club. Because as it stands, Pledges might not be horrible - there's nothing unbalanced or broken about them - but they're so underwhelming that there's really no reason to interact with them except as a barrier standing between you and the story. Very little stick, and even less carrot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, could we maybe not trash talk subsystems like this? Respect other people's preferences is a forum rule, and &quot;I'm glad to hear the previous developer is gone, hopefully his work will be replaced with something that doesn't suck&quot; is really pushing the limits of that rule. Especially given that David's departure from Onyx Path and the replacement of his work on Changeling is still very much a sensitive subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T17:34:36-07:00","id":1148475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges#post1148179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or is the Pledges subsystem for Lost 2e extremely neutered from what 1e had to offer?</div> </div> </div> </div> Its just you. Well, not just you. Lots of pepole are under this gross misunderstanding. <br /> <br /> You see, Goblin Vows are a type of pledge. And, if what blackhatmatt said is true and very little changed? Dear gods, they are so brokenly, insanely, mindblowingly powerful. You can get insane benefits for your PC, and if you do it right, the costs are very easy to deal with. I honestly think that these are actually STRONGER than 1e's pledge system. Hells, I personally think that Goblin Vows put Awakened Creative Thaumaturgy to shame.<br /> <br /> Sealings are extremely potent, especially if you back them with a Contract. You can casually bind someone's words, no need to balance things out or math. Just someone says something, you seal it, you put a Contract in just in case to give it oomph. Its scary. I once saw a Sealing bound with Control Elements. You automatically take 4L a turn from breaking the sealing and getting Inferno raging around you (I presume it lasts the scene). That's mean. You do not want to break a sealing. They're scary powerful.<br /> <br /> Now, Oaths I'm not really excited about. I've had three different motleys during my time with the playtest, and the benefits don't WOW me. All in all, its roughly equivalent to a one dot merit. That said, they're all useful benefits that come up often- free dot of mantle, +1 to hedgesploration are both very relevant to virtually every session. Getting personalized motley and personal oath benefits are pretty good too, when you look at the possibilities - sharing social dice pools, sharing health and willpower tracks... while not as outrageously powerful as a sealing or goblin vow, the utility and ability to coordinate together as a group is nothing to sneeze at, and can be very strong.<br /> <br /> Bargains seem the odd man out. The benefits are hard to measure, though, because we don't have a full grasp of how Huntsmen work. From the times I encountered them, though? Being able to hide long enough to come up with an ambush is pretty good. Or get a full 8 hours sleep before running. It comes down to how your ST runs the Huntsmen, though, so its open question. All in all, though, if bargains aren't your thing, th<br /> <br /> The only thing that I want that's not included? Granting access to magic or abilities to mortals through a pledge. There's no way to act as a middle man between a goblin vow and a secondary person, for instance. But if you just measure a single changeling PC? Scary powerful.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Not neutered at all. In fact, they've been given steroids. You just have to know how to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T21:32:01-07:00","id":1148514,"title":"","content":"Between the fact that it's trivially easy for any kind of Changeling, Huntsman, or any other fae creature to ignore any attempt at a Sealing outright, I'd call them of similarly trivial importance/use. Any target of merit would have to practically walk intentionally into a situation in order to run afoul of one. Sure, there are a few Contracts which can levy some rather nasty consequences, but in-character the motivations for ever allowing it to get that far are nonexistent - especially when it's called out in the fluff writeup that refusal to accept a Sealing isn't even seen as any kind of faux pas or indication of dishonesty.<br /> <br /> And Bargains? You only apply a -1 to be tracked per separate Bargain that you sign on for. If you want to get that penalty high enough to appreciably hide you from a Huntsman, you're going to be filling Bargains as the equivalent of a full-time job, since each individual Bargain is on the order of spending one day a week cleaning someone's house, or sewing a new outfit for someone every month. Between that and the fact that all of these Bargains have to be made with mortals whom you're showing your Mien instead of your Mask - there's no real pretending that this isn't some kind of crazy magical something-or-another going - and sure, you might hypothetically be able to avoid your Huntsman this way, but it's going to ruin any kind of masquerade you had going on the mortal side of things, and it's going to eat up a tremendous amount of your character's free time performing menial tasks for mortals to make it happen.<br /> <br /> They're not exactly useless, but at the same time the incentives to accept/employ them in play just aren't there. Sealing needs either a carrot or a stick to reward accepting/punish refusing one, and you need way too many Bargains going at once to get an appreciable benefit from all the time and energy you'll be investing into them.<br /> <br /> Oaths are kind of their own thing entirely - a hoop to jump through to join a Court/Freehold/Motley (or any other kind of magical organization, like a Noble Order) - and they're fine in that role. The carrot is membership, in that case, and not the super minor boon - and the stick is that it's permanent, one way or another. Not useful as a mechanical tool so much as a narrative threshold, indicating a permanent allegiance that your character's volunteered for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T00:31:32-07:00","id":1148538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148514#post1148514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the fact that it's trivially easy for any kind of Changeling, Huntsman, or any other fae creature to ignore any attempt at a Sealing outright, I'd call them of similarly trivial importance/use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen can't ignore Sealings on account of not having Glamour and a point of Glamour you spend on getting out of a Sealing is a point that you don't have for later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to get that penalty high enough to appreciably hide you from a Huntsman, you're going to be filling Bargains as the equivalent of a full-time job, since each individual Bargain is on the order of spending one day a week cleaning someone's house, or sewing a new outfit for someone every month.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> you need way too many Bargains going at once to get an appreciable benefit from all the time and energy you'll be investing into them. </div> </div> </div>\u2026This is a bucket-of-dice-game problem, isn't it.<br /> <br /> Three Bargains imposes a penalty equivalent to the highest conventionally-encountered difficulties for a normal action. That's three jobs that are <i>usually</i> \u2014 and thus by implication <i>not necessarily</i> \u2014 ongoing tasks equivalent to lending a hand on the regular in ways that you can explicitly delegate. The penalty a Bargain applies is distinguished from the penalty being in a Hollow imposes on similar rolls by only working against Huntsmen but not requiring you to be in a specific place, and the most readily available means of setting up a Bargain involves a universal ability that can be combined with a related universal ability that causes mortal witnesses to remember a scene as though it were a dream, to say nothing of the more roundabout option of making the deal in dreams.<br /> <br /> Huntsmen are statted as mortals with a lot of Experiences and get no bonuses to tracking changelings that aren't predicated on having an Icon \u2014 three dice on top of any other penalties you can throw at it is nothing to sneeze at, considering that higher Wyrd specifically makes it easier for fae things like the Huntsmen to track you and your primary alternatives for the same benefit are going off the grid and/or living in a very well-furnished barrow for the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> In practical terms, a Bargain is no more strenuous to the narrative than vampires running feeding scenes or mages engaging in ritual casting or Iron Masters using Sounds of the City to shut down Social Merits \u2014 it's a scene of effort in the course of the larger story that connects to the wider world. You're not obligated to make Bargains, but they serve a useful function to the game regardless of how little the equivalent of free Merits and a chance to show off your character's strong points impresses you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T02:03:22-07:00","id":1148546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148538#post1148538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen can't ignore Sealings on account of not having Glamour and a point of Glamour you spend on getting out of a Sealing is a point that you don't have for later.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand the point of Death of a Thousands Cuts. Problem is a single cut isn\u00b4 t going to make much of a difference.<br /> Now, if a violated Sealing would have instead a continuous &quot;bleeding&quot; effect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-10-2017, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T08:36:17-07:00","id":1148594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148546#post1148546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the point of Death of a Thousands Cuts. Problem is a single cut isn\u00b4 t going to make much of a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>A single cut divorced from context, sure.<br /> <br /> Volumes have been written about how little worth there is in divorcing things from their context in these games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, if a violated Sealing would have instead a continuous &quot;bleeding&quot; effect... </div> </div> </div>Then it would be rendered nonsensical in the framework of &quot;spending Glamour means this word-binding doesn't take.&quot; If your goal is to turn changelings who break their word into serial dramaturges, this would be appropriate, but as it stands it's supposed to be a way to hold characters to their word and therefore speak carefully. I've had &quot;your maximum Glamour pool gets set to zero for a week&quot; as a yet-untriggered consequence of breaking an Oath \u2014 I would not apply an analogous consequence to something as low-stakes as a Sealing.<br /> <br /> You could make it so that stopping a Sealing from settling altogether costs Willpower and spending Glamour at the time of breakage allows you to instead buy off one breakage per point, but that then all but necessitates a limit on how many Sealings you can keep up at once or how long they last, because otherwise you can apply an indefinite number of drains that last for literally as long as you want.<br /> <br /> We're talking about changelings, here. Lots of little advantages stacked here and there is in-theme for universal powers. Glamour-poison and lump-sum deductions are the bailiwick of more involved pledgecraft and Contract work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T11:37:28-07:00","id":1148644,"title":"","content":"....<br /> <br /> Well, I like the pledge system. Thank you Black Hat Matt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-10-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T14:42:20-07:00","id":1148685,"title":"","content":"Me too! <br /> <br /> Maybe because I don't have any baggage associated with how Sealings worked in 1e, but I liked the in-universe acknowledgement and that they typically were pretty low-cost and minor, but can be used to all sorts of interesting effects. Hell, knowing my players (I am heavily leaning towards Changeling 2e being our first Chronicles of Darkness game), they would manage to find sorts of ways of using those seemingly minor magical effects to great effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:34:09-07:00","id":1149747,"title":"","content":"As with many things about 2nd edition, I'm finding less poetry and magic in the Pledge system than in the older rules. I feel like, as cumbersome as the old system could be, it offered a greater versatility to players and Storytellers. The current rules feel...reduced into the three most common uses for pledges. It feels constraining and rigid in a way the older system did not. Early days, of course, so the criticism might not apply when the full game is released. But first impressions are what we're talking about, and that was mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T11:57:47-07:00","id":1149969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1149747#post1149747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with many things about 2nd edition, I'm finding less poetry and magic in the Pledge system than in the older rules. I feel like, as cumbersome as the old system could be, it offered a greater versatility to players and Storytellers. The current rules feel...reduced into the three most common uses for pledges. It feels constraining and rigid in a way the older system did not. Early days, of course, so the criticism might not apply when the full game is released. But first impressions are what we're talking about, and that was mine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This may also be a function of having half the word count that the first edition had, which is, in turn, a function of having to reprint 30,000 words of core rules in every book rather than saying &quot;see the CofD book&quot;. Write your Congressperson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T13:58:28-07:00","id":1150202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1149969#post1149969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This may also be a function of having half the word count that the first edition had, which is, in turn, a function of having to reprint 30,000 words of core rules in every book rather than saying &quot;see the CofD book&quot;. Write your Congressperson.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, this is punchier than I meant it to be. Lemme clarify some things.<br /> <br /> I probably could have asked for more word count between one version of CtL2nd and the other, but frankly I feel like the pledge system works as written. I <i>could</i> fill more words, and if we do a sourcebook where it's appropriate to tease out the topic, I'd totally write more about it. But in a core book, where word count is always stretched thin, you want to have enough words to cover the important stuff and set up places to expand later. <br /> <br /> On the subject of core rules in the core &quot;fatsplats,&quot; I personally don't like it. I thought that the decision of having a core book to refer to and dedicating the fatsplats to their character type was a good one, but I understand why it changed. I'm still gonna grumble about it, as it my wont, but don't actually write your Congressperson (rather, do, but not about this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T07:55:17-07:00","id":1150353,"title":"","content":"1e pledges were also clunkier and difficult to use. It was very difficult to get the equivalent of a sealing, because you always had to balance it. Let alone having to stop the game and do math. I hate doing maths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:08:46-07:00","id":1150370,"title":"","content":"The fact that you cannot grant any kind of magical boons to anyone without a permanent, life-long, unending Oath is the iron nail in the coffin for me. Sure, you can get bonuses for yourself with Goblin Pledges, but you can't actually grant them to other people. No Sealing someone's promise in such a way that they get bonuses to complete their tasks instead of just penalties for failure. No granting mortals boons as long as they follow whatever fae requirements you set forth for them (and quite the opposite in the Bargains category, really, where you do mundane drudgery for mortals in exchange for similarly trivial benefits).<br /> <br /> That's the real loss of utility in the Pledge system. There are plenty of sticks, but vanishingly few carrots to incentivize using them in the first place. Being able to apply Goblin Pledge boons to ordinary Sealings should go a long way towards fixing that. And so, too, would being able to swear Oaths with a fixed duration instead of them being ways to join a Motley or a Court for literally the entire rest of your life.<br /> <br /> You know, make them an actual tool, instead of just an onus placed on anyone foolish enough to commit verbally to something, or anyone who wants to join a magical social club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:39:51-07:00","id":1150380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1150370#post1150370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you cannot grant any kind of magical boons to anyone without a permanent, life-long, unending Oath is the iron nail in the coffin for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about a game whose magic items have, from day one, been described as commonplace, regularly-used, and possessed of inescapable prices. It is just possible changeling pledgecraft has never been about cost-free bennies from nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No granting mortals boons as long as they follow whatever fae requirements you set forth for them (and quite the opposite in the Bargains category, really, where you do mundane drudgery for mortals in exchange for similarly trivial benefits). </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mundane drudgery&quot; like &quot;Lend them your magic furniture&quot; or &quot;Keep their dreams clear of incubi&quot; or &quot;Send your buddy over to have a talk with their landlord&quot;? Social networking may not be the spotlight material of a Changeling game, but making trades of all sorts is a sufficiently constant background activity that an excuse to dedicate a scene or two to its maintenance now and again is fine and dandy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And so, too, would being able to swear Oaths with a fixed duration instead of them being ways to join a Motley or a Court for literally the entire rest of your life. </div> </div> </div>&quot;You can't have not sworn this Oath&quot; is not &quot;You can't leave the group you swore this Oath for.&quot; It establishes a relationship that continues to affect its constituents as long as they all live, but having an exit cost isn't the same as Court membership being a Simpsons meme. That unbroken Oath in my game? It's got an effective term of less than a month. It's still going to translate to my player's character having made a mutual agreement with the oldest Duchess in the freehold, but once the full moon rolls around he's not in danger of starving to death unless he fails to pay back the last favor on his tab.<br /> <br /> Please maintain a sense of perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T06:57:18-07:00","id":1150626,"title":"","content":"So... one nail = final and only nail. Got it.<br /> <br /> Let me show you just how easy it is to fix that.<br /> <br /> New Goblin Contract: Middle-Man<br /> Activation: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Politics + Wyrd<br /> Cost: 1 glamour, 1 willpower<br /> Dramatic Failure: The changeling has to bear the cost of the Vow, while target gets all the benefit<br /> Failure: No agreement reached<br /> Success: The changeling successfully serves as a middle man between a Goblin Vow they possess, and a chosen target / second party. The target gains all the benefits of the Vow, but also must fulfill any cost associated with the Vow.<br /> Exceptional Success: The changeling gets the benefit as well as the target at no extra cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or make a house rule to let you seal the goblin vow as part of a regular sealing. Or bargain. Tada. Done.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't hard to do. Its trivial. You don't like it, house rule it. There's at least ten ways I can think of to do what you want, depending on how you want it done. <br /> <br /> A changeling swearing to obey his Court's Crown and getting benefits? All changelings of Mantle 2 get a goblin vow related to their court, and swearing to fulfill a command can very well be done by swearing on the Court's goblin vow aspect. Tada, there's your benefit, its and entirely temporary. <br /> <br /> Honestly, at this point, I really have to ask if you've actually used any of these in play, or you're just reacting based on the pledges not being as OMG broken as they were in 1e. Change happens. Have you tried them out in play to see how well they work for you in actual experience? I don't get that feeling - most people that do tend to start talking about the actual experience they have with it being difficult, rather than how things are theoretically difficult. <br /> <br /> I'm playing in a changeling game right now. I personally haven't Sealed anyone (mostly because I don't have the need to, but that's always been true of me, even when I played CtL 1e), but my motley-mates have. I've done bargains and oaths plenty - freehold, motley, court, and two personal, and I'm happy with the results. I'm the witch of the group, so I've invested a lot in Goblin Vows, and can usually arrange for one of the five I have to do something for almost any given situation with some bargaining. Based on my experiences, the pledge system is currently very easy to use, user friendly, and doesn't make the game stop as people figure out if everything in a pledge balances out. <br /> <br /> Speaking of, that need to balance things in the old 1e pledges actually made sealings all but impossible, imho. That time our Ifrit sealed someone with their Contract? That ease would have been impossible - we'd have had to stop the game, think of the right way to phrase things, and that just DRAGGED the game. And then, we'd have had other fae, who are in the know, be just as careful with the words back, and it would all amount to nothing anyways. Pledges, more often than not, ended up as nothing more than a circle jerk of people buffing themselves up. And 2e pledges don't work that way, no. But they do have some interesting uses that are fun and easy to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-18-2017, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T07:57:07-07:00","id":1150642,"title":"","content":"eh. the new pledge rules leave me a little cold but not so much as to dampen my excitement for the new edition of the game. pledgecraft was never a huge aspect of any of the changeling games that i ran. most of the time i would just handwave their creation, as one could easily spend half an hour or more fiddling around with the various aspects of the oath and that is boring.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T16:03:01-07:00","id":1150819,"title":"","content":"I think the only real problem with the new system as written is the limitations on &quot;type&quot; of who can swear what type of pledge. As long as one individual has an attachment to the Wyrd or Arcadia, any type of pledge should be available. The limitation just feels unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 10-18-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T16:17:14-07:00","id":1151780,"title":"","content":"When Sealings are avoidable with a single point of Glamour, your GM is, at best, patronizing you when they have enemies submit to an inconvenient Sealing.<br /> <br /> And requiring a homebrewed Contract in order to bestow a boon on a Pledge means that the base system as written is more than a little anemic. Needing homebrew just to give it some functional punch is the key sign of a system with problems.<br /> <br /> Oaths, as they stand - being permanent magical bindings - serve almost exclusively as a hoop to jump through while joining a Freehold, Court, or Motley. Their benefits are almost nonexistent - the boons they grant are, at best, minor conveniences - and instead serve primarily as a magical onus keeping you from ever betraying - or even <b>quitting </b>- the group to which you've <b>permanently</b> committed the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> Goblin Vows are the one real exception - something that has actual utility in use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Mundane drudgery&quot; like &quot;Lend them your magic furniture&quot; or &quot;Keep their dreams clear of incubi&quot; or &quot;Send your buddy over to have a talk with their landlord&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Mundane drudgery like:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bargain is usually an ongoing task \u2014 a changeling might offer to clean the human\u2019s house once a week, or sew her a dress once a month, or grant her pleasing dreams three nights a week. </div> </div> </div>Obnoxious time sinks that, in terms of narrative and flow of story, only eat up your character's down time and make them less-available for Motley activities. In exchange for performing ongoing, menial work for a mortal, Huntsmen take a tiny penalty to actively track you down.<br /> <br /> The thing that especially ruins Bargains, though, is this little fact:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No matter the nature of the other party, the changeling must appear to him without her Mask, and propose the bargain. </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but blowing your identity as a faerie monster to a mortal is, alone, not worth the benefit offered by a Bargain, let alone adding grunt work performed for them on top of that.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Pledge system remains that Sealings have almost no reason to actually be used when they're so easily ignored, and Oaths/Bargains have a whole lot of risk/stick for the changeling enacting them, but a dreadful lack of reward/carrot for that same changeling, meaning that there's no motivation to interact with them outside of what's absolutely necessary. Goblin Vows are the exception - because they offer an actual carrot to the equation - but all of the other types should have similarly baked-in motivation for employing them. They don't - and 'homebrew it until it isn't a problem anymore' doesn't change that the base system is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T16:45:17-07:00","id":1151787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1151780#post1151780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Sealings are avoidable with a single point of Glamour, your GM is, at best, patronizing you when they have enemies submit to an inconvenient Sealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's suddenly patronizing to have an enemy accept a Sealing to add an element of scrutiny to the things they say or do? A tenth of a starting character's fuel capacity is trivial? Resource management involving small costs does not make it costless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oaths, as they stand - being permanent magical bindings - serve almost exclusively as a hoop to jump through while joining a Freehold, Court, or Motley. Their benefits are almost nonexistent - the boons they grant are, at best, minor conveniences - and instead serve primarily as a magical onus <u>keeping you from ever betraying - or even <b>quitting </b>- the group to which you've <b>permanently</b> committed the rest of your life.</u> </div> </div> </div>Did that thing I pointed out about how &quot;the connection is permanent&quot; doesn't mean &quot;the connection bears the same context forever&quot; go unnoticed or are we pretended that that doesn't matter for the sake of more trash-talk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obnoxious time sinks that, in terms of narrative and flow of story, only eat up your character's down time and make them less-available for Motley activities. </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you think &quot;motley activities&quot; are? Because they're certainly not <i>your entire life</i>, barring specific examples formed for a purpose that takes that kind of commitment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In exchange for performing ongoing, menial work for a mortal, Huntsmen take a tiny penalty to actively track you down. </div> </div> </div>You are explicitly allowed to delegate or use your magic powers to facilitate your end of the bargain and a -1 penalty is equivalent to a one-dot Merit on top of the favors the mortal end can offer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know about you, but blowing your identity as a faerie monster to a mortal is, alone, not worth the benefit offered by a Bargain, let alone adding grunt work performed for them on top of that. </div> </div> </div>Again: Dreams count, half-remembered supernatural encounters qualify, nothing about the setup necessitates or implies throwing a Bargain up on a whim is how they operate, and a -1 penalty is also flush with the benefits offered in 1e by <i>belonging to a freehold and adhering to its attendant strictures</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with the Pledge system remains that Sealings have almost no reason to actually be used when they're so easily ignored, and Oaths/Bargains have a whole lot of risk/stick for the changeling enacting them, but a dreadful lack of reward/carrot for that same changeling, meaning that there's no motivation to interact with them outside of what's absolutely necessary. </div> </div> </div>&quot;What's absolutely necessary&quot; <i>is the narrative function of pledgecraft</i>. Nothing about the previous edition's system's implied use-intent is contradicted by the system put forth in 2e \u2014 changelings didn't put up offers for good dreams to complete strangers willy-nilly, nor did they tend to invoke the lasting partnership of a motley or a Court for particularly short terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Goblin Vows are the exception - because they offer an actual carrot to the equation - but all of the other types should have similarly baked-in motivation for employing them. They don't - and 'homebrew it until it isn't a problem anymore' doesn't change that the base system is a problem. </div> </div> </div>The importance of wording is as much &quot;homebrew&quot; here as it was in the previous edition. Swearing an Oath or making a Bargain means you agree to the terms you offer \u2014 and that includes time limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:23:54-07:00","id":1152044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did that thing I pointed out about how &quot;the connection is permanent&quot; doesn't mean &quot;the connection bears the same context forever&quot; go unnoticed or are we pretended that that doesn't matter for the sake of more trash-talk? </div> </div> </div>In the text, the only way to recontextualize the Oath you're bound up in is to pick up Oathbreaker by leaving or defaulting on your current Oath. Meaning that if you decide you want to leave your Court or your Freehold, you have to go around and make restitution to each and every individual member of your Court or your Freehold, and then make restitution with the Wyrd itself before you lose the Oathbreaker penalty.<br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, but what's written doesn't actually support you. The contexts provided are 'still in the good graces of the Oath you swore' or 'you're an Oathbreaker and it's going to be an entire campaign worth of hoops to jump through before you're not eating penalties for that.'<br /> <br /> No finite duration. No escape clauses. Just being forever bound by the onus of an Oath until such a time as you're willing to suffer the trial by fire to escape from the lifelong commitment you made.<br /> <br /> You're making things up and adding them to the rules because, frankly, they need them. They're extremely punishing, compared to the extremely minor incentives for actually interacting with them. They're extremely punishing in several places, rewarding in almost none of them, and completely toothless everywhere else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:48:21-07:00","id":1152049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148644#post1148644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....<br /> <br /> Well, I like the pledge system. Thank you Black Hat Matt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much likewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:55:27-07:00","id":1152050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1152044#post1152044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're making things up and adding them to the rules because, frankly, they need them.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The specific examples of what an oath can involve include <b>the conditions of victory in a duel</b>.</i><br /> <br /> If &quot;oaths are circumscribed by their wording&quot; is me making something up \u2014 despite &quot;the consequences of breaking an oath are usually laid out in the oath itself and are usually extremely bad if left to chance&quot; being in the text \u2014 then &quot;the conditions of an oath beyond the establishment of a relationship have no finite duration and last forever regardless of wording&quot; is a flagrant lie.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, man, it's hard to take your assessments in good faith when the non-voluntary consequences of the Oathbreaker Condition are about as intense as the Bargain benefits you keep saying are underwhelming. I said at the start that this was the main reason nobody was eager to do this thread a third time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T19:40:13-07:00","id":1152093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1149969#post1149969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This may also be a function of having half the word count that the first edition had, which is, in turn, a function of having to reprint 30,000 words of core rules in every book rather than saying &quot;see the CofD book&quot;. Write your Congressperson.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wait, all I can say here is huh? I haven't really had a load of time to sit down and read any of the 2nd Edition stuff save for Beast: The Primordial and I tried to read Werewolf and Vampire but every time I get started I end up getting sidetracked on one thing or another. <br /> <br /> Why is stuff from the core book having to be reprinted in each game? I think one of the things they did for NWoD that I thought was smart was to put all of the rules that effected everyone exactly the same all into one book, this cut down on word count in each game or gave ya'll more word count to play with and expand on things. It also did my favorite thing. It cut down/eliminated the contradictions [It's okay....I'll wait for you to recover from the revelation that the OWoD games often not only contradicted one another, but even contradicted their own gameline]. <br /> <br /> I'm I understanding that statment right that their going backwards, using up word space for something that really only needed to be printed in one book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T00:05:03-07:00","id":1152130,"title":"","content":"It means you only need 1 book to play. 1 book is cheaper than 2 books. If you're never going to run a mortals game, then you don't need to buy an extra book just to play the game you were interested in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T10:42:09-07:00","id":1152229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1148301#post1148301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote pledges, both the original version that David developed and the current version that Rose/Meghan developed. Very little changed. Sorry if you don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for the update. I actually like sealing, they function well as simply minor curses, tricks, prank, and a minor social binding agent when Oaths are over kill.<br /> <br /> Oaths mean something now, they are forever, when you put a ring on it, that really means forever. It is also the reason why Wyrd no longer effects how many pledges you can have.<br /> <br /> Bargains are interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T02:59:13-07:00","id":1152738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1152229#post1152229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the update. I actually like sealing, they function well as simply minor curses, tricks, prank, and a minor social binding agent when Oaths are over kill.<br /> <br /> Oaths mean something now, they are forever, when you put a ring on it, that really means forever. It is also the reason why Wyrd no longer effects how many pledges you can have.<br /> <br /> Bargains are interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, I miss the flexibility of the previous system regarding duration and sanction.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look to the old Good Neighbour Pact: &quot; Let's have a truce for a year and a day. The one who breaks it will become defenseless against the other&quot;. This is a good example of a pledge focused in a particular purpose, with a medium duration and a reasonable cost for the oathbreaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-25-2017, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T08:26:50-07:00","id":1152811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1152738#post1152738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, I miss the flexibility of the previous system regarding duration and sanction.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look to the old Good Neighbour Pact: &quot; Let's have a truce for a year and a day. The one who breaks it will become defenseless against the other&quot;. This is a good example of a pledge focused in a particular purpose, with a medium duration and a reasonable cost for the oathbreaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>That flexibility is still there. The contents of that oath I've been mentioning amount to &quot;If one of us helps the other between now and the next full moon, they have to return the favor or lose their Glamour retention for a week.&quot; You couldn't do disproportionate durations of task and sanction in the old system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:20:15-07:00","id":1153110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1148179-2e-pledges?p=1152738#post1152738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I miss the flexibility of the previous system regarding duration and sanction.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look to the old Good Neighbour Pact: &quot; Let's have a truce for a year and a day. The one who breaks it will become defenseless against the other&quot;. This is a good example of a pledge focused in a particular purpose, with a medium duration and a reasonable cost for the oathbreaker.</div> </div> </div> </div> Still works as an Oath. <br /> <br /> Oaths aren't permanent. They permanently mark a changeling, yes, but that's different from being permanent. Take a look at the Court Oaths. You can still leave a Court. You'll forever be branded as a former member of Court X, but you won't be bound by the terms of the Oath at all. Its just a footnote really, one that makes up your personal story. <br /> <br /> So, what we have here is the Good Neighbor Pact working as a Personal Oath. You agree to a ceasefire / truce for a year. Or, honestly, for whatever duration you dang well please. Unlike the old pledge, you can make it end after a conflict is wrapped up, you can make it end after a time period, you can set the ending point for when the final season of Game of Thrones finishes airing on HBO or even when both sides mutually agree its over. If either breaks the Oath while its active, they'll suffer the Oathbreaker Condition, which includes Contracts failing to work. So, yes, the oathbreaker would naturally be unable to defend themselves against the victim here. <br /> <br /> This is how you handle a new Good Neighbor Pact. Its even easier than in 1e, since there's no need to crack open the book at all when doing it. No balancing, no referencing. No need to even use legalese. Just roleplay the actual agreement out, and go separate ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T10:36:14-07:00","id":1153218,"title":"","content":"I like this. I really tried to like the old system and I really liked the flavour of it. But in practice it ended up with a bunch of time lost, a bunch of notepaper notes of the balance and then no one ever using pledges again because they didn't want to go through with it all. This has the same flavour and same effects with less math and hassle which overall enriches the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}